# The pilot's frozen corpus is content-addressed: run_pilot.py checks its
# sha256 against a digest pinned in the source, and refuses on a mismatch.
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would
# rewrite every LF to CRLF on checkout and change those bytes -- so a fresh
# clone would fail the digest check on a file nobody had touched.
# -text pins the bytes in both directions.
experiments/002-pilot-tiny-ttt/corpus.txt -text

# Shell scripts must check out with LF even on Windows. Several of these are
# pasted into Google Cloud Shell or run under WSL, and a CRLF shebang fails
# there as `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` -- an error that
# names neither the file nor line endings, on a script that runs fine locally.
*.sh text eol=lf
